<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="{{ csp }}">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="referrer" content="no-referrer">
<title>Analytics Health: {{ run.rsid_name or run.rsid }} {{ run.today }}</title>
<style>
{{ css }}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header class="page-head">
  <div class="head-row">
    <h1>Analytics Health Dashboard</h1>
    <div class="theme-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Color theme">
      <button type="button" data-theme-choice="auto" aria-pressed="true" title="Follow the computer's setting">Auto</button>
      <button type="button" data-theme-choice="light" aria-pressed="false">Light</button>
      <button type="button" data-theme-choice="dark" aria-pressed="false">Dark</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <dl class="facts">
    <div><dt>Report suite</dt><dd>{{ run.rsid_name or run.rsid }} <span class="muted">({{ run.rsid }})</span></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Individual component</dt><dd>{{ individual_label }}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Segment</dt><dd>{% if run.segment_id %}{{ run.segment_id }}{% else %}None (all visits){% endif %}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Run date</dt><dd>{{ run.today }} <span class="muted">(report suite time zone {{ run.timezone }})</span></dd></div>
    <div><dt>Run time</dt><dd>{% if run.started_at %}{{ run.started_at[:16] | replace("T", " ") }} <span class="muted">(time on the computer that ran it)</span>{% if run.duration %}<br>Took {{ run.duration }}{% endif %}{% else %}Unknown{% endif %}</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Status</dt><dd><span class="badge badge-{{ status_kind }}"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">{{ status_icon }}</span>{{ status_label }}</span></dd></div>
  </dl>
  {% if last_day %}<p class="hint" id="date-note"><strong>Run date set with --date.</strong> Every day in this report counts back from the run date, so the last day is {{ last_day }}.</p>{% endif %}
</header>

<div class="change-alert">
  <div class="sliders">
  <label for="change-alert">Large drop alert: flag changes below</label>
  <input type="range" id="change-alert" min="-100" max="-10" step="5" value="-{{ change_alert_pct }}" aria-valuetext="-{{ change_alert_pct }}%" aria-describedby="change-alert-hint">
  <output for="change-alert" id="change-alert-value">-{{ change_alert_pct }}%</output>
  <span>from the weekday average</span>
  <label for="spike-alert">Large spike alert: flag changes above</label>
  <input type="range" id="spike-alert" min="10" max="200" step="10" value="{{ spike_alert_pct }}" aria-valuetext="+{{ spike_alert_pct }}%" aria-describedby="change-alert-hint">
  <output for="spike-alert" id="spike-alert-value">+{{ spike_alert_pct }}%</output>
  <span>from the weekday average</span>
  </div>
  <p class="change-alert-result" id="change-alert-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p class="change-alert-result" id="spike-alert-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
  <p class="hint" id="change-alert-hint">The weekday average is the average of the same weekday in the 12 weeks before the day.</p>
  <details class="rule" id="change-alert-rule">
    <summary>How large drops and spikes are found</summary>
    <ul>
      <li>The weekday average for a day is the average of the same weekday in the 12 weeks before it, e.g., the 12 Mondays before a Monday.</li>
      <li>A value is a large drop when its change from the weekday average is below the drop slider's setting, e.g., below -30%. Move the slider left to flag only deeper drops.</li>
      <li>A value is a large spike when its change from the weekday average is above the spike slider's setting, e.g., above +50%. Move the slider right to flag only bigger spikes. A value that doubled is about +100%.</li>
      <li>Components with a weekday average under {{ min_usual }} are skipped, because small numbers change a lot from day to day.</li>
      <li>A value of 0 is not a large drop. It is listed as "Dropped to zero".</li>
      <li>A value that Adobe flagged is listed as an unusual value, not as a large drop or spike.</li>
      <li>A large drop gets a "Large drop" badge in the Flag column, a large spike gets a "Large spike" badge, and both are listed on the Alerts tab.</li>
      <li>The tables show a down arrow for a change past the drop slider, and an up arrow for a change past the spike slider.</li>
    </ul>
  </details>
</div>

<section class="tiles" id="tiles" aria-label="{{ last_day ~ ' at a glance' if last_day else 'Yesterday at a glance' }}"></section>

<section class="status-section{% if not component_drops and not issue_groups %} status-ok{% endif %}" id="status" aria-labelledby="status-title">
  {% if component_drops or issue_groups %}
  <h2 id="status-title">Status</h2>
  {% endif %}
  {% if component_drops %}
  <div class="warning" id="component-drops">
    <p class="issue-heading"><span class="badge badge-flag"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">!</span>Warning</span> This run sees fewer components than the run before it.</p>
    <ul class="issue-items">
      {% for d in component_drops %}
      <li>{{ d.message }}</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
    <p class="warning-cause">{{ component_drop_cause }}</p>
  </div>
  {% endif %}
  {% if issue_groups %}
  <p>Some data could not be read in this run. Each item below says what is missing and why.</p>
  <div class="copy-row">
    <button type="button" id="copy-problems">Copy problems</button>
    <span id="copy-problems-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
  </div>
  <ul class="issues">
    {% for g in issue_groups %}
    <li class="issue">
      {% if g.heading %}
      <p class="issue-heading">{{ g.heading }}</p>
      {% else %}
      <p class="issue-heading">Problem code <code>{{ g.code }}</code>{% if g.entries | length > 1 %} ({{ g.entries | length }} items){% endif %}</p>
      {% endif %}
      {% set show_items = not g.heading or g.entries | selectattr("component_id") | list %}
      {% if show_items %}
      <details{% if g.entries | length <= 3 %} open{% endif %}>
        <summary>{% if g.entries | length == 1 %}Details{% else %}Details for {{ g.entries | length }} items{% endif %}</summary>
        <ul class="issue-items">
          {% for it in g.entries %}
          <li>{% if it.component_id %}<code>{{ it.component_id }}</code>: {% endif %}{{ it.message }}</li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </details>
      {% endif %}
    </li>
    {% endfor %}
  </ul>
  {% else %}
  {% if component_drops %}
  <p class="status-line"><span class="badge badge-good"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>No problems</span>No problems were found in this run.</p>
  {% else %}
  <div class="status-line"><h2 id="status-title">Status</h2><span class="badge badge-good"><span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>No problems</span><span class="hide-narrow">No problems were found in this run.</span></div>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}
</section>

<nav class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Report sections">
  <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-components" aria-controls="panel-components" aria-selected="true">Components Summary</button>
  <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-individual" aria-controls="panel-individual" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Individual Component Summary</button>
  <button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-alerts" aria-controls="panel-alerts" aria-selected="false" tabindex="-1">Alerts Summary</button>
</nav>

<main>
<section class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-components" aria-labelledby="tab-components">
  <div class="controls">
    <label>Show
      <select id="granularity">
        <option value="day">Daily</option>
        <option value="week">Weekly</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <label id="day-label">Day
      <select id="day"></select>
    </label>
    <label>Custom components
      <select id="range">
        <option value="">All</option>
      </select>
    </label>
    <label class="check" id="flagged-label"><input type="checkbox" id="flagged-only"> Show only flagged</label>
  </div>
  <p class="note" id="week-note" hidden>{{ week_note }}</p>

  <details class="fold calendar-card" open>
    <summary><h2 id="calendar-title">Alerts by day, last 13 weeks</h2></summary>
    <p class="hint">Each square is one day. A darker square had more components that Adobe flagged or that dropped to zero. Large drops and spikes are not counted, because only the last 7 days have a weekday average. Choose a day to list its components, and choose one to see it on the chart.</p>
    <div id="calendar"></div>
  </details>

  <details class="fold charts-fold" open>
  <summary><h2 id="charts-title">Charts</h2></summary>
  <div class="charts">
    <figure class="chart-card">
      <div class="picker-row">
        <label class="picker-type">Type
          <select id="metric-type">
            <option value="">All</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label class="picker-main">Metric chart <select id="metric-pick"></select></label>
      </div>
      <div class="chart" id="metric-chart"></div>
    </figure>
    <figure class="chart-card">
      <div class="picker-row">
        <label class="picker-type">Type
          <select id="dimension-type">
            <option value="">All</option>
            <option value="evars">eVars</option>
            <option value="props">Props</option>
            <option value="other">Other</option>
          </select>
        </label>
        <label class="picker-main">Dimension chart <select id="dimension-pick"></select></label>
      </div>
      <div class="chart" id="dimension-chart"></div>
    </figure>
  </div>
  </details>

  <div class="table-tools">
    <label>Find a component
      <input type="search" id="find" placeholder="Name, number or ID" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false">
    </label>
    <p class="hint">The line in each row shows the last 13 weeks, with a dot on the chosen day. Choose a line to see the component on its chart above.</p>
  </div>
  <div id="tables"></div>
</section>

<section class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-individual" aria-labelledby="tab-individual" hidden>
  <div class="controls">
    <label>Dimension
      <select id="pair-dimension"></select>
    </label>
    <label>Metric
      <select id="pair-metric"></select>
    </label>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">The dropdowns list the pairs stored in this run. To add another pair to this run, run <code>ahd individual --run {{ run.id }} --dimension "&lt;name or ID&gt;" --metric "&lt;name or ID&gt;"</code>. Add the same <code>--profile</code> or <code>--db</code> option that you used for the run, so that it finds the same database. It takes a few seconds and writes this report again.</p>
  <h2 id="individual-title"></h2>
  <figure class="chart-card wide">
    <figcaption id="individual-caption"></figcaption>
    <div class="chart" id="individual-chart"></div>
  </figure>
  <p class="hint">The line on the chart marks the day chosen with the Day picker on the Components Summary tab. The weekly view marks no day.</p>
  <details class="fold" open>
  <summary><h2 id="top100-title">Top 100 values {{ day_words }}</h2></summary>
  <p class="hint">Movement compares the rank with the previous 90 days. For example, "up 3" means the value is 3 places higher than before. A dash means no change. "* new" means the value is new to the top 100.</p>
  <div id="top100"></div>
  </details>
  <details class="fold" open>
  <summary><h2 id="browser-title">Browser analysis</h2></summary>
  <p class="hint">Top 10 values {{ day_words }} for each major browser group.</p>
  <div id="browser"></div>
  <p class="hint">{{ breakdown_notes.browser }}</p>
  </details>
  <details class="fold" open>
  <summary><h2 id="device-title">Device analysis</h2></summary>
  <p class="hint">Top 10 values {{ day_words }} for each device type. Desktop traffic falls under Other.</p>
  <div id="device"></div>
  <p class="hint">{{ breakdown_notes.device }}</p>
  </details>
</section>

<section class="panel" role="tabpanel" id="panel-alerts" aria-labelledby="tab-alerts" hidden>
  <h2>Alerts</h2>
  <div class="controls">
    <label>Day
      <select id="alert-day"></select>
    </label>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">Components that Adobe flagged as unusual, that fell further below or rose further above their weekday average than the sliders allow, or that dropped to 0.</p>
  <div class="copy-row">
    <button type="button" id="copy-alerts">Copy alerts</button>
    <span id="copy-result" role="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
  </div>
  <p class="hint">Days in a row counts the days, up to the chosen day, that had the same alert. The report covers 7 days, so a count that reaches the first of them says "or more".</p>
  <p class="hint">The copy holds a formatted table and plain text. An email program such as Outlook or Gmail pastes the table, and a chat or text editor pastes the text.</p>
  <div id="alerts"></div>
  <details class="copy-fallback">
    <summary>Show the alert summary as text</summary>
    <textarea id="alert-text" readonly rows="8" aria-label="Alert summary as text"></textarea>
  </details>
  <details class="fold declines" open>
    <summary><h2 id="declines-title">Slow declines</h2></summary>
    <p class="hint">Components whose weekly totals fell by {{ decline_pct }} percent or more a week for the last {{ decline_weeks }} weeks. No single day falls far enough for an alert, so the lists above miss them. This list does not count as alerts. Each week ends on the weekday of the last day checked, so each week has every weekday once.</p>
    <p class="hint">Steady is 1 when the weekly totals fall in a straight line, and 0 when they jump around. The list leaves out components below {{ decline_fit }}.</p>
    <div id="declines" data-weeks="{{ decline_weeks }}"></div>
  </details>
  <details class="fold history" open>
    <summary><h2 id="history-title">Earlier runs</h2></summary>
    <p class="hint">The alerts on the last day of each run of this report suite{% if run.segment_id %} and segment{% endif %} in the database, newest first, up to {{ history_runs }} runs. Every run is counted by the rules of this report, and large drops and spikes follow the sliders. Runs for later dates are not listed.</p>
    <div id="history"></div>
  </details>
</section>
</main>

<footer class="page-foot muted">Made by ahd {{ run.tool_version }}, run {{ run.id }}. This page loads nothing from the internet.</footer>

<template id="no-bands-template"><p class="note chart-note">{{ no_bands_note }}</p></template>
<script type="application/json" id="data">{{ data }}</script>
<script>
{{ js }}
</script>
</body>
</html>
